# Goal: navigate to target_pose, optionally passing through waypoints (in
# order) first. Any concrete navigation stack (Nav2, a custom planner, a
# simple point-and-shoot driver, ...) expresses itself through this same
# interface; stack-specific knobs (behavior tree file, planner/controller
# plugin id, ...) go in parameters_json.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped target_pose
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped[] waypoints
string parameters_json
---
# Result
# Shared result-code convention across Navigation/Manipulation/Perception
# (0-9 reserved for the shared block, capability-specific codes start at 10;
# documented convention, not enforced by the type system, since actions
# cannot share constants across files).
uint16 SUCCESS=0
uint16 REJECTED=1
uint16 ABORTED=2
uint16 CANCELED=3
uint16 TIMEOUT=4
uint16 NO_PATH_FOUND=10
uint16 LOCALIZATION_LOST=11
uint16 error_code
string error_msg
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped final_pose
builtin_interfaces/Duration total_time
---
# Feedback
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped current_pose
builtin_interfaces/Duration navigation_time
builtin_interfaces/Duration estimated_time_remaining
float32 distance_remaining
int16 number_of_recoveries
uint32 current_waypoint_index
